QA Dashboard APT package
========================

This package installs the Electron application under /usr/lib/qa-dashboard
and the desktop launcher /usr/bin/qa-dashboard. Electron is bundled, so the
package has no Node.js/npm runtime dependency.

QA Sentinels is recommended, not a hard dependency. Its /usr/bin/qa wrapper
uses an existing ~/QA-Sentinels checkout or seeds a per-user workspace on
first use. You can install the packages separately:

  apt install qa-sentinels                 # engine only
  apt install qa-sentinels qa-dashboard    # engine + GUI
  apt install --no-install-recommends qa-dashboard  # GUI only; no engine

The License & Legal window is a read-only compliance register. License and
third-party notices are installed under /usr/share/doc/qa-dashboard.

QA Dashboard is only a front end and has no monitoring or evidence-collection
code of its own. Without qa-sentinels it starts, but its Sentinels windows have
nothing to read or invoke. The package does not install a cron/systemd
schedule itself; QA Dashboard keeps its fallback cycle when neither is
present.

The source installer also provides a hidden GNOME theme extension for the
favourite icon. The APT package intentionally omits it; the application works
without it.
